ARM64EC: the C runtime's scalar math functions keep the JIT's FPCR too

0043 lists the native functions nothing FPCR's AH, NEP or trap enables change can run in, which excluded every
function with a floating-point instruction. What was left of the two FPCR writes per call on Microsoft Flight
Simulator's main thread (5.9 % of its time after 0043, squark records 25.77) is the C runtime's math functions: cos,
atan2, fmod, powf, acos, modf, sin, log, pow, tanf, exp, about 256,000 calls a second in the cockpit.

Their arithmetic is scalar (add, multiply, divide, fused multiply-add, square root, compares, conversions, rounding),
and a scalar result's low lane is the same value with or without the JIT's bits: NEP only changes what the
instruction leaves above the low lane of its destination; AH changes fmax/fmin on NaNs and zeros and the estimate
instructions (never allowed), the sign of a generated default NaN (negative, as on x86), when tininess is detected
(after rounding, as on x86), and it makes fabs and fneg leave a NaN alone, sign included. The last one does change
values: compilers build the mask 0x7fff... as fneg of all-ones, and a negative NaN that keeps its sign through fabs
can miss an exponent check further on (log, cbrt, _copysign and hypot came out different in squark-private's
mathsweep.c). So fpcrscan.py lists a second class, with bit 0 of the RVA set, only for the exports of ucrtbase and
msvcrt named in its SCALAR_ALLOW (43 and 32 functions), when nothing they reach does vector floating-point
arithmetic or looks above the low lane of a register a scalar instruction wrote, and only those mathsweep.c found
equal in value, NaN count and errno with and without the JIT's bits (special values, NaNs of both signs, every
exponent, three MXCSR modes). msvcrt's math_error ends a path (Wine patch 0073).

- AddTableTargets inserts a marked RVA as address | 1. Hash() ignores bit 0, so both kinds probe from the same slot.
- ExitFunctionEC: a probe that finds target | 1 reads FPCR and keeps it only when no trap enable is armed (IOE DZE
  OFE UFE IXE IDE, set while the guest has an exception unmasked in MXCSR); otherwise it writes FPCR as for an
  unlisted target. Unmarked entries are as before: no read.
- SQUARK_FEX_FPCR_SCALAR=0 leaves the marked entries out; SQUARK_FEX_FPCR_TABLE=0 the whole table, as before.

Per x64 call under FEX in a loop (M5 Max): cos 30.4 -> 6.9 ns, sin 30.6 -> 8.0, atan2 36.8 -> 9.1, fmod 28.2 -> 7.8,
powf 41.7 -> 7.6, acos 47.4 -> 11.0, modf 26.2 -> 5.0, exp 34.7 -> 7.6, sqrt 25.9 -> 5.6, floor 25.9 -> 5.5,
pow 41.7 -> 18.4. Results that are NaN for a reason of the function's own (acos(2), fmod(x, 0)) are now negative
NaNs, as on x86; nothing else changes.

A table without marked RVAs (0043's fpcrscan.py) behaves exactly as before.

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
@@ -58,7 +58,9 @@
   // A target in FPCRNeutralHash (squark 0036, 0043; Module.cpp) is not affected by the JIT's FPCR bits, so it runs
   // with them: writing FPCR here and again on the way back costs more than most such calls. Open addressing with
   // linear probing over 1 << 15 slots, 0 ends a probe, 1 is a removed entry. x16, x17 and x23 are free here (all three
-  // are overwritten below before use); eor, ubfx, add, and, sub and cbz leave NZCV alone.
+  // are overwritten below before use); eor, ubfx, add, and, orr, sub, cbz and cbnz leave NZCV alone.
+  // An entry with bit 0 set (squark 0044) is a function that does scalar floating-point arithmetic: AH and NEP do
+  // not change its values, an armed trap enable could make it trap, so it keeps the JIT's FPCR only while none is.
   eor x16, x9, x9, lsr #15
   ubfx x16, x16, #2, #15
   adrp x17, FPCRNeutralHash
@@ -68,9 +70,17 @@
   cbz x23, 3f
   sub x23, x23, x9
   cbz x23, 1f
+  sub x23, x23, #1
+  cbz x23, 4f
   add x16, x16, #1
   and x16, x16, #0x7fff
   b 2b
+4:
+  mrs x17, fpcr
+  and x16, x17, #0x1f00 // IOE DZE OFE UFE IXE
+  and x23, x17, #0x8000 // IDE
+  orr x16, x16, x23
+  cbz x16, 1f
 3:
   // Clear any the AFP NEP and AH bits in FPCR as native code won't expect their behaviour.
   mrs x17, fpcr
diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -478,6 +478,10 @@
 //   TimeDateStamp and .text size are the ones scanned. Calls into Wine's syscall and unix call dispatchers, its debug
 //   output and its ARM64EC syscall wrappers are allowed because Wine patch 0070 drops the JIT's bits there, and calls
 //   into FEX's own exports because they do too (FPCRFence below). SQUARK_FEX_FPCR_TABLE=0 leaves the table out.
+//   squark 0044: an RVA with bit 0 set is a function whose floating-point arithmetic is scalar only and never looked
+//   at above the low lane (the C runtime's math functions: fpcrscan.py's "scalar functions"). AH and NEP leave its
+//   values alone; it goes in with bit 0 set and ExitFunctionEC keeps the JIT's FPCR for it unless a trap enable is
+//   armed. SQUARK_FEX_FPCR_SCALAR=0 leaves these out.
 // Inserted under ThreadCreationMutex (image map), read without a lock by ExitFunctionEC.
 constexpr uint64_t Slots = std::size(FPCRNeutralHash);
 static_assert(Slots == (1 << 15), "Module.S masks with 0x7fff");
@@ -528,6 +532,14 @@
   return Enabled;
 }
 
+bool ScalarEnabled() {
+  static const bool Enabled = [] {
+    const char* Setting = std::getenv("SQUARK_FEX_FPCR_SCALAR");
+    return !Setting || strcmp(Setting, "0");
+  }();
+  return Enabled;
+}
+
 bool NameIs(std::string_view ModuleName, std::string_view Name) {
   return ModuleName.size() == Name.size() &&
          std::equal(Name.begin(), Name.end(), ModuleName.begin(), [](char a, char b) { return a == std::tolower(b); });
@@ -553,11 +565,21 @@
       LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: {} is not the build FPCRNeutralTable was made from, no entries", ModuleName);
       continue;
     }
-    size_t Added = 0;
-    for (size_t i = 0; i < Entry.Count; i++) {
-      Added += Insert(Address + Entry.RVAs[i]);
+    size_t Added = 0, Scalar = 0;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < Entry.Count; i++) {
+      const uint32_t RVA = Entry.RVAs[i];
+      if (RVA & 1) {
+        if (ScalarEnabled()) {
+          const bool New = Insert((Address + (RVA & ~3u)) | 1);
+          Added += New;
+          Scalar += New;
+        }
+        continue;
+      }
+      Added += Insert(Address + RVA);
     }
-    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: {} {} functions keep the JIT's FPCR ({} slots used)", ModuleName, Added, Used);
+    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: {} {} functions keep the JIT's FPCR, {} of them scalar floating point ({} slots used)", ModuleName,
+                      Added, Scalar, Used);
   }
 }
